@31 = ~Hello. My master is looking for powerful adventurers like you to accompany him on an experiment. Are you interested?~
@32 = ~ Who's your master? ~
@33 = ~ What kind of experience? ~
@34 = ~ My master's name is Telim'Gar. ~
@35 = ~ An experience about the inner strength inherent in all those who know how to rise to challenges. ~
@36 = ~Okay, but what kind of experience is it?~
@37 = ~All right. How can I help?~
@38 = ~Without more information, I'll pass. Goodbye.~
@39 = ~If you want to help the master, you must first prove your power by completing the challenges.~
@310 = ~Which challenges?~
@311 = ~I propose the challenges, you choose. Each challenge sends you “elsewhere” and you must return with a magic rune to prove your victory.~
@312 = ~A magic rune?~
@313 = ~Yes, a magic rune.~
@314 = ~All right, propose your challenges, golem.~
@315 = ~In that case, no thanks. I'm leaving.~
@316 = ~The Dump.~
@317 = ~The Silent necropolis.~
@318 = ~The Vegetable labyrinth.~
@319 = ~The Steel tombs.~
@320 = ~The Maze.~
@321 = ~Supramaginium.~
@322 = ~The Furnace.~
@323 = ~The Tomb of the Great worm.~
@324 = ~The Playroom of the Evil.~
@325 = ~The Pocket of normality.~
@326 = ~The Library.~
@327 = ~That's it? No details, no explanations?~
@328 = ~Explanations: already given. Details: no.~
@329 = ~Hello. My master is looking for powerful adventurers like you to accompany him on an experiment. You cheated by leaving a challenge without the corresponding rune. The master knows this and refuses to receive you.~
@330 = ~Hello. My master is looking for powerful adventurers like you to accompany him on an experiment. You have proven your power. You may meet the master.~
@331 = ~The Forge.~
@332 = ~What challenge do you want to take on?~
@333 = ~Actually, I'll come back later.~
@334 = ~Never mind, just suggest the challenges I still have left to try.~
@335 = ~Then I'm leaving.~
@336 = ~Okay, let's go.~
@337 = ~Maybe later.~
@338 = ~Hello. My master is looking for powerful adventurers like you to accompany him on an experiment. You have defeated the master, so you'll have to wait a decade for him to rebuild his challenges.~
@339 = ~Hello. My master is looking for powerful adventurers like you to accompany him on an experiment. You have started the experiment. Would you like to continue?~
@340 = ~Yes, show me the challenges I still have to attempt.~
@341 = ~What are the Library, the Museum of the Dead, and the Pasture?~
@342 = ~*The golem stares at you without reacting for a few seconds before responding* You do not have access to the Library.~
@343 = ~Okay, but what about the Museum of the Dead and the Pasture?~
@344 = ~I have no information on that.~

